{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788112101,"nonce":"NW8OVUV2cnViRscXPzVDcbWf0+I=","title":"1.2 Journal: events.ndjson event stream","message":"Wave 1 — substrate. Depends: 1.1.\n\n## Goal\nThe journal: append-only events.ndjson — \"what the player saw while time ran\".\nSubstrate for digests (2.1), watchpoints (1.3), post-mortems (4.1), and rwtest\nassertions (5.1).\n\n## Context (read first)\n- DESIGN.md §Journal §Observation model\n- `logrelay/Source/RelaySink.cs` + Patches.cs (log capture; decide integrate\n  vs coexist — no double-capture of errors)\n- decompiled: LetterStack, Messages, Alert/AlertsReadout, Pawn_HealthTracker\n  notify paths, MentalStateHandler\n\n## Scope\n- Events (each: seq, gameTick, wallTime, type, payload): letter (def, label,\n  text, lookTargets), message, alert_on/alert_off (id, label, severity),\n  death, downed, mental_break (pawn, state), red_error, warning (deduped),\n  dev (provenance of every dev:* verb, written by 3.1), session markers\n  (game loaded/saved/newgame).\n- Capture via read-only Harmony postfixes on notify paths; alerts via\n  cadenced readout scan (they have no notify event) — cadence configurable.\n- Rotation: one file per game session under journal/; `journal` verb: read\n  since seq/tick with type filter (also directly tail-able from shell).\n- Schema documented in-repo (rwtest depends on field stability).\n\n## Invariants\nAppend-only; hooks are observers (no behavior change, no Rand, no lazy-gen);\nbounded cost (no per-tick scans besides the alert cadence; measure).\n\n## Open questions (worker's)\nExact hook points; alert scan cadence; warning dedupe policy; whether job\nfailures are worth an event type in v1.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Scripted sequence (dev raid incident + forced letter + induced red error +\n  pawn downed) produces correctly ordered, correctly stamped events.\n- Journal survives save/load round-trip without duplication or gap.\n- Overhead measured negligible via AnalyzerBridge/DPA on a running colony.","files":null}]}